                <pb facs="0573" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.2315/166: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Poindexter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-26T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                                1925—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Ambassador Rio telegraphs instructions being sent Brazilian Chargé to sign
                    Procès Verbal and that Brazilian Minister in Lima is also being advised to this
                    effect for information of Peruvian Government. Colombian Minister already
                    authorized to sign. Please endeavor to have instructions sent Peruvian
                    Ambassador so that Procès Verbal may be signed Saturday<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d285-f1"/> if possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
